From fc9611fc8a00002b7f58b62513dcfbf5389768b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:34:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ask_contact drops a quality word the owner never wrote
 instead of refusing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tester's 58044 (0267, day one): 2 of 3 day-one sends reached the
75 s mark only after refused tries. In three days, 9 of the 14
fact-keeping refusals on ask_contact were a quality word the owner never
wrote („სანდო"), each costing a whole model round before the same ask
went again.

The server now drops that one word itself before the checks, as it
already does in the owner's reply (4456, withoutQualityNotSaid). Every
other fact check (who it is for, a time, a bracketed detail, a quoted
owner's line) stays a refusal. No model-facing text changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HwFREQwL5g9E6qRrUf9bau
---
